# Solid Project specifications.
#
# Source: https://solidproject.org/TR/
# Snapshot: 2026-11-23.
#
# The W3C API does not expose the Solid Community Group's Technical Reports,
# so the 26 work items listed on the TR page are curated here. Test suites
# (Test Suite, Specification Tests) are not specifications and are excluded.
# The notification channel types appear twice on the TR page (in the Technical
# Reports and in the channel-type table); each is recorded once.
#
# "Use W3C data whenever possible": the Solid Community Group itself is the
# existing W3C group <https://www.w3.org/community/solid/> (see groups.ttl), and
# editors below reuse the W3C person identities already in data/identities.json
# instead of creating duplicate people. Names without a W3C identity are
# omitted rather than invented. The W3C display name for elf Pavlik is
# "Pavlik elf", and Maxime Lecoq-Gaillard is recorded as "Maxime Lecoq"; the
# GitHub identifiers in data/identities.json confirm both matches.
#
# Published reports use ex:landingPage; editor's drafts use ex:editorDraft.
# bibo:status keeps the TR page's current stage verbatim.
#
# The Solid-PREP subject carries a #solid-prep fragment so its UI route key
# stays unique; the document path ends in /protocol/, which would otherwise
# collide with the Solid Protocol route. ex:editorDraft is the real document
# URL.
#
# The Shape Trees entry uses the current GitHub Pages rendering named by the
# specification's own metadata. The TR page still links the older
# https://shapetrees.org/TR/specification/ URL, which now serves unrelated
# content. The Authorization Use Cases Survey is a Markdown document in the
# authorization panel repository, without a rendered editor list.
#
# Seeded with `devbox run seed -- static` (see scripts/fuseki.ts).

@prefix ex: <http://example.org#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix bibo: <http://purl.org/ontology/bibo/> .

